# BOOT WITH ADDON of Hello.gba with RESET on, as a page will start it
# (actions.c, through the menu's test hook, tests/nav.sh): as the launch
# starts on its addons, the loading card shows the game's name and "Loading
# the game", which it keeps through the quick checks (save states,
# patches): they move the bar and are only logged (source/progress.h). The
# other switches' slots are erased, and its log line says they are off
# (v0.3.2: 65535, the erased slot's value); Hello's cheat file picks Max
# money, whose two byte writes put the cheat hook in.
#! settings 1=1
-w "nav: home ready"
-P "@8:nav_test_path:/Hello.gba" -p @8:nav_test_action:0x7E000002
-w "BOOT WITH ADDON: reset 1, savestate 0, sleep 0, cheats 1 (2)"
-s @0:addons.png
